      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Christopher! I think than in the final stage it would make sense to have the RUST_ICC build flag to exclude the skcms_Parse and call the rust implementation when enabled. However, as we are still in experimental phase, for the first stage I think it would be safer to duplicate the MakeICCProfile method so that we can explicitly call it from specific codecs: initially RustBMP, then we can go for RustPNG and after that we probably could cleanup the new method and just modify MakeICCProfile as I mention, something like this:\n\n```\nstd::unique_ptr\u003cColorProfile\u003e ColorProfile::MakeICCProfile(\n        sk_sp\u003cconst SkData\u003e data) {\n    if (data) {\n        skcms_ICCProfile profile;\n#if defined(SK_CODEC_COLOR_PROFILE_PARSE_WITH_RUST)\n        rust_icc::ICCProfile rust_profile;\n        if (rust_icc::parse_icc_profile(\n                    rust_icc::ToRustSpan(data-\u003ebyteSpan()), \u0026rust_profile)) {\n                rust_icc::ToSkcmsICCProfile(rust_profile, \u0026profile);\n                return std::unique_ptr\u003cColorProfile\u003e(\n                        new ColorProfile(profile, std::move(data)));\n        }\n#else     \n        if (skcms_Parse(data-\u003edata(), data-\u003esize(), \u0026profile)) {\n            return std::unique_ptr\u003cColorProfile\u003e(new ColorProfile(profile, std::move(data)));\n        }\n#endif\n    }\n    \n    return nullptr;\n}\n```",
